{"id": "EUVD-2026-108767", "enisaUuid": "8eeb45ac-46f1-3881-a83c-1fa5268c25f0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/bridge: Fix unlocked list_del in drm_bridge_add()\n\nWhen re-adding a bridge that was previously removed, drm_bridge_add()\ndrops it from bridge_lingering_list without holding bridge_lock.\n\nBoth bridge_list and bridge_lingering_list are protected by bridge_lock,\nas they are concurrently modified by drm_bridge_remove() and\n__drm_bridge_free(), and walked by the debugfs 'bridges' file.  Running\nthe list_empty() test and the list_del_init() outside of the lock may\ntherefore corrupt either list.\n\nPerform both under bridge_lock.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:19:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:19:46", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f469d850854101eae60dd4080244f114a9bcf2b5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b62e3db8cdc1680e1c3390591e872f485148541a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98973"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "17bb1834-1c5d-3342-859d-7a74e1973238", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "2753ddf4-9cb7-3ffe-baaf-9ad58cab7407", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.19"}, {"id": "628baaca-c788-3b1d-b768-7205754a2525", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "17805a15d1751f5d6bb06f924f9bed216feb8db7 <f469d850854101eae60dd4080244f114a9bcf2b5"}, {"id": "b42186d4-e2a5-3c4c-a69d-b97ff860a950", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "17805a15d1751f5d6bb06f924f9bed216feb8db7 <b62e3db8cdc1680e1c3390591e872f485148541a"}, {"id": "d7164836-0a53-364a-bdfc-d48b283df9c6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "d812fda7-6c9d-3544-8fb4-4e5c5f48be4d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9dbd8a20-1814-3b64-82ec-647c599a5762", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}